      "title": "Grounds for discipline",
      "narration": "Section 10-126 lists what can cost Theo his license. Making an intentional material misstatement on a license application. Obtaining or trying to obtain a license through fraud. Violating the Insurance Article or a Commissioner’s order. Misappropriating, converting or unlawfully withholding money belonging to an insurer, insured or applicant. Intentionally misrepresenting the terms of a policy. Forging an insurance document. Being convicted of a felony or a crime of moral turpitude. Demonstrating a lack of trustworthiness or competence. Failing to obey a lawful order or subpoena. Having a license disciplined in another state. Failing to report as required. Any of these supports action against the license.",
