      "title": "Suspension, revocation and reapplication",
      "text": "A suspension ends on its stated date, and the producer resumes without reapplying, provided renewal and education duties were met. A revocation ends the license entirely; the former licensee may apply again only after the period the Commissioner sets and must show rehabilitation. A refusal to renew has the same practical effect as revocation.",
